{"name":"Scarlet Ibis","hex":"#f4601b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scarlet ibis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brightly scarlet, migratory species of ibis, of species Eudocimus ruber, of South America and the Caribbean."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarlet_ibis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scarlet ibis","blocks":[{"text":"The scarlet ibis, sometimes called red ibis, is a species of ibis in the bird family Threskiornithidae. It inhabits tropical South America and part of the Caribbean. In form, it resembles most of the other twenty-seven extant species of ibis, but its remarkably brilliant scarlet coloration makes it unmistakable. It is one of the two national birds of Trinidad and Tobago, and its Tupi–Guarani name, guará, is part of the name of several municipalities along the coast of Brazil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Oceanografic_Scarlet_Ibis_02.jpg/330px-Oceanografic_Scarlet_Ibis_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_ibis"},{"title":"Ibis","blocks":[{"text":"The ibis are a group of long-legged wading birds in the family Threskiornithidae that inhabit wetlands, forests and plains. \"Ibis\" derives from the Latin and Ancient Greek word for this group of birds. It also occurs in the scientific name of the western cattle egret mistakenly identified in 1757 as being the sacred ibis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Black-headed_Ibis_%28Threskiornis_melanocephalus%29.jpg/330px-Black-headed_Ibis_%28Threskiornis_melanocephalus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibis"},{"title":"Scarlet (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Scarlet is a bright red color, sometimes with a slightly orange tinge. In the spectrum of visible light, and on the traditional color wheel, it is one-quarter of the way between red and orange, slightly less orange than vermilion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/52/RCMP-female-officer.jpg/330px-RCMP-female-officer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Scarlet_Ibis_juvenile_RWD.jpg/500px-Scarlet_Ibis_juvenile_RWD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Scarlet_Ibis_juvenile_RWD.jpg/1280px-Scarlet_Ibis_juvenile_RWD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Scarlet_Ibis_juvenile_RWD.jpg/500px-Scarlet_Ibis_juvenile_RWD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An older juvenile with a touch of red","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScarlet_Ibis_juvenile_RWD.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Guar%C3%A1_alta.jpg/500px-Guar%C3%A1_alta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Guar%C3%A1_alta.jpg/1280px-Guar%C3%A1_alta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Guar%C3%A1_alta.jpg/500px-Guar%C3%A1_alta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Taxidermy specimen","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuar%C3%A1_alta.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Scarlet_Ibis_skull_%E2%80%9CEudocimus_ruber%E2%80%9D_at_MAV-USP.jpg/500px-Scarlet_Ibis_skull_%E2%80%9CEudocimus_ruber%E2%80%9D_at_MAV-USP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.